The M340 module now pulls SNMP data using Schneider Electric's Transparent Ready private MIB (``TFPRIVATE-MIB``, compiled without the MIB texts), with proper data types, enumeration labels and decoded table indices, walking the equipment profile (including the LED and trap tables), Port 502 messaging, I/O scanning, Global Data, web, address server, NTP and email groups that the agent advertises, plus ``ifTable`` and ``ipAddrTable``. The results fill in the device's interfaces, services, module status, uptime and related peer IPs (the full data is in ``extra.snmp``), values the MIB can't decode are kept as raw OIDs instead of aborting the pull, and the pull stops walking once the agent stops responding. The new ``m340.use_snmp`` and ``m340.snmp_max_varbinds`` device options turn off all SNMP requests to M340 devices (e.g. for devices affected by CVE-2022-0222) and limit the number of requests. ``peat.protocols.snmp.SNMP`` gained ``load_mibs()``, ``walk()``, ``get_table()``, ``last_error`` and ``timed_out``, and responses now include the typed ``value``, ``table`` and ``index_parts`` of each object.
